================================================================================
DEMO 4: HIRING — Detecting interviewer disagreements via cycles
================================================================================

BoostRanker | 10 observations | 4 items
================================================================================

Rank |         Item | Combined |   Inert | Ramified |   Split |         Type
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
   1 |        Alice |    +0.64 |    +0.0 |    +1.27 |   -2.31 | UNPREDICTABLE
   2 |        Carol |    +0.52 |    +1.0 |    +1.04 |   +0.42 |     BALANCED
   3 |          Bob |    +0.23 |    +1.0 |    +0.46 |   +1.98 | UNPREDICTABLE
   4 |         Dave |    -1.39 |    -2.0 |    -2.77 |   -0.08 |     BALANCED

ANOMALIES (upsets):
  Obs #5: Carol beat Alice (surprise=92%, margin=60%)
  Obs #9: Bob beat Alice (surprise=87%, margin=50%)
  Obs #8: Bob beat Carol (surprise=64%, margin=50%)

CYCLES DETECTED (3):
  Bob > Carol > Alice > Bob
  Dave > Bob > Alice > Dave
  Dave > Bob > Carol > Dave

INTERPRETATION:
  Cycles indicate interviewer DISAGREEMENT, not candidate ambiguity.
  The SPLIT channel score tells you which candidates are most
  contentious (high |split|) vs consensus picks (low |split|).

  Alice: CONTENTIOUS (split=-0.39) — interviewers disagree
  Dave: CONSENSUS (split=-0.02) — interviewers agree
  Bob: CONTENTIOUS (split=+0.40) — interviewers disagree
  Carol: CONSENSUS (split=+0.08) — interviewers agree

